<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Software Application Font on Typophile Archive</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/software-application-font/</link><description>Recent content in Software Application Font on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 26 Apr 2008 22:15:00 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/software-application-font/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Macromedia</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/44707/</link><pubDate>Sat, 26 Apr 2008 22:15:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/44707/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140731010037/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Indices"&gt;Indices&lt;/a&gt; : &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140731010037/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Companies"&gt;Companies&lt;/a&gt; : Macromedia&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Macromedia was a software company based in &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140731010037/http:/typophile.com/wiki/San%20Francisco"&gt;San Francisco&lt;/a&gt; California that published the popular &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140731010037/http:/typophile.com/wiki/type%20design"&gt;type design&lt;/a&gt; application &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140731010037/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Fontographer"&gt;Fontographer&lt;/a&gt;. The company was acquired by &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140731010037/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Adobe"&gt;Adobe&lt;/a&gt; in 2006.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Macromedia was a On May 9 2005 &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140731010037/http:/typophile.com/wiki/FontLab%20Ltd."&gt;FontLab&lt;/a&gt; announced the licensing of the full &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140731010037/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Fontographer"&gt;Fontographer&lt;/a&gt; product line from Macromedia Inc. and its further development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;UK designer &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140731010037/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Neville%20Brody"&gt;Neville Brody&lt;/a&gt; has received notoriety in part due to his graphic design systems, including custom &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140731010037/http:/typophile.com/wiki/type%20desgn"&gt;type desgn&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140731010037/http:/typophile.com/wiki/typography"&gt;typography&lt;/a&gt; for Macromedia during the 1990s.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>